<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Madison returns six weeks after the diagnosis. He finished the levetiracetam taper three weeks ago; his events have not increased, and the irritability has gone. He has had four psychotherapy sessions and keeps his event diary: three events in six weeks, each shorter than before, all at the end of long study days or after poor sleep. He has begun to notice a warning feeling of distance and heaviness, and once stopped an event by grounding himself. He understands and accepts the diagnosis, and has explained it to two friends. His mood is still low most mornings and he worries a great deal about his examinations; he would like help beyond the therapy. He has had no thoughts of death or self-harm, and the rifle remains locked. He has not driven. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Events</td><td>Three in six weeks, shorter; one stopped by grounding</td></tr><tr><td>Levetiracetam</td><td>Stopped three weeks ago; no rebound; irritability gone</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Four sessions</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9 and GAD-7</td><td>11 and 12</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts; rifle locked; not driving</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

