<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Functional/dissociative seizures (F44.5)</content>. Fewer and shorter events after four sessions, and he is learning to recognize and interrupt them; no rebound after stopping levetiracetam, which confirms that it was not needed. [S]<list><item>Continue the twelve psychotherapy sessions and the diary.</item><item>Still not driving; the three-month event-free interval has not started.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Taking an antiseizure medicine without a confirmed diagnosis (Z79.899)</content>. Resolved: levetiracetam stopped three weeks ago. [S]<list><item>No antiseizure medicine; a note on his record and emergency card asks that typical events not be treated with benzodiazepines or antiseizure medicines.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate (F32.1)</content>. PHQ-9 11, little changed from 13 at intake despite psychotherapy; item 9 scored 0. Shared decision to add an SSRI, which helps depression and anxiety; in the LaFrance trial sertraline alone did not reduce events, so psychotherapy remains the main treatment for the seizures. [S]<list><item>Sertraline 25 mg each morning for one week, then 50 mg.</item><item>Nurse telephone check in two weeks for side effects and safety.</item><item>Safety plan reviewed; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Generalized anxiety disorder (F41.1)</content>. GAD-7 12, down from 14. [S]<list><item>Sertraline as above; worry and examination anxiety addressed in therapy.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9</td><td>Baseline, then at least monthly during acute treatment; every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>11, down from 13 at intake; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>GAD-7</td><td>With the PHQ-9 when anxiety accompanies depression</td><td>Completed today</td><td>12, down from 14</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9)</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior; rifle locked; protective factors unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Event diary: frequency, duration, triggers, warning sensations, and injuries</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Three events in six weeks, shorter, linked to long study days and poor sleep; one interrupted by grounding; no injuries</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antiseizure medicine review</td><td>At diagnosis and until withdrawn</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taper completed three weeks ago with no rebound in events</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>SSRI tolerability check two weeks after starting</td><td>2 weeks after starting and after each dose change</td><td>Due</td><td>Sertraline starts today; nurse telephone check booked for two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>CBT-informed psychotherapy for functional seizures</td><td>Weekly during the course</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Four of twelve sessions attended</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Driving</td><td>Every visit until cleared</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Not driving</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sleep, studies, and first-aid plan</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sleeping about six and a half hours; agreed to stop studying by 10 pm; testing accommodations requested</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lithium, anticonvulsant mood-stabilizer, or antipsychotic monitoring</td><td>Only on those drugs</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not taking any; no bipolar features</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Cause of the episodes established by the second visit. Outcome by 2026-04-30: Functional/dissociative seizures documented by video-EEG; epilepsy and syncope excluded [S]</item><item>Antiseizure medicine stopped safely. Outcome by 2026-06-11: Levetiracetam tapered over three weeks and stopped, with no change in events and less irritability [S]</item><item>Events reduced by at least half, then free of events for three months. In progress; target 2026-12-31 [S]</item><item>Depression and anxiety improved by at least 50 percent (PHQ-9 and GAD-7). In progress; target 2026-12-31 [S]</item><item>No suicidal thoughts. In progress; target 2026-12-31 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Hingray C, et al. Functional/dissociative seizures: Proposal for a new diagnostic label and definition by the ILAE task force. Epilepsia 2025;66(11):4162-4182 (PMID 40884444) (2025); LaFrance WC Jr, et al. Multicenter pilot treatment trial for psychogenic nonepileptic seizures: a randomized clinical trial. JAMA Psychiatry 2014;71(9):997-1005 (PMID 24989152) (2014); Goldstein LH, et al. Cognitive behavioural therapy for adults with dissociative seizures (CODES): a pragmatic, multicentre, randomised controlled trial. Lancet Psychiatry 2020;7(6):491-505 (PMID 32445688) (2020); Tolchin B, et al. Seizures, Driver Licensure, and Medical Reporting Update: An AAN Position Statement. Neurology 2025;104(7):e213459 (PMID 40073306) (2025); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Nurse telephone check in two weeks; preventive visit next month; three-month review. Next scheduled visit 2026-07-16: preventive health visit at 23. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
